<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/ob3> a owl:Ontology , prof:Profile ;
    dct:title "Open Badges 3.0 — credential SHACL profile"@en ;
    dct:description "SHACL shapes for a 1EdTech Open Badges 3.0 credential — a W3C Verifiable Credential (VC Data Model 2.0) whose subject carries an achievement — the checks Foxxi applies to the credentials it issues and accepts. A profile of Open Badges 3.0: the shapes target 1EdTech's own classes and constrain the predicates the OB 3.0 and VC 2.0 JSON-LD contexts map a credential to, and each requirement is OB 3.0's (its data model, Appendix B)."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by 1EdTech or W3C. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "Since 2026.10.0 the shapes target 1EdTech's classes and the VC 2.0 predicates; the classes and properties this document had minted for them are deprecated."@en ,
        "A credential typed AchievementCredential is an OpenBadgeCredential here: OB 3.0's context maps both names to ob:OpenBadgeCredential."@en ,
        "Achievement criteria are read with ob:Criteria, the IRI OB 3.0's context maps the criteria property to (the vocabulary's Criteria class has the same IRI)."@en ,
        "Earlier publications served this document's terms under https://interego-foxxi-bridge.livelysky-8b81abb0.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io/ns/ob3#, on a host since retired. A term IRI in that namespace names the term with the same local name in this one; the Foxxi validator reads it so, and nothing is published there any more."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/ob3/2026.10.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "2026.10.0" ;
    skos:historyNote "Versioned by calendar (YYYY.MM.PATCH) from 2026.10.0: the version numbers this document, not the standard it formalizes. Every released version stays resolvable at its version IRI, and the content there never changes. Earlier publications carried no version IRI, and their owl:versionInfo restated the version of the standard."@en ;
    dct:creator "Mark Spivey" ;
